{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0007561","label":"multiple epiphyseal dysplasia type 1","definition":"Multiple epiphyseal dysplasia type 1 (MED 1) is a form of multiple epiphyseal dysplasia that is characterized by normal or mild short stature, pain in the hips and/or knees, progressive deformity of extremities and early-onset osteoarthrosis. Specific features to MED 1 include a more pronounced involvement of hip joints and gait abnormality and a shorter adult height. MED1 is allelic to pseudoachondroplasia with which it shares clinical and radiological features. The disease follows an autosomal dominant mode of transmission.","synonyms":["COMP multiple epiphyseal dysplasia (disease)","EDM1","MED1","Polyepiphyseal dysplasia type 1","epiphyseal dysplasia multiple 1","epiphyseal dysplasia, multiple, 1","epiphyseal dysplasia, multiple, type 1","multiple epiphyseal dysplasia (disease) caused by mutation in COMP"],"xrefs":["DOID:0070303","GARD:0002180","MEDGEN:325376","OMIM:132400","Orphanet:93308","SCTID:715673002","UMLS:C1838280","icd11.foundation:2130489957"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":3,"is_group":false,"n_genes":1,"n_phenotypes":36,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[{"id":"e_de1063e8112b","source":"MONDO:0007561","target":"COMP","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:93308","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/93308","confidence":0.95,"snippet":"Disease-causing germline mutation(s) in (Assessed) — cartilage oligomeric matrix protein"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:93308","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"url":"https://hpo.jax.org/browse/disease/ORPHA:93308","snippet":"COMP is annotated as disease gene of ORPHA:93308 (HPO genes_to_phenotype, Orphanet-derived)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.95,"independent_sources":["Orphanet"],"level":"curated"}],"phenotypes":[{"edge":{"id":